/how-votes-are-counted"},{"date":"2 days ago","position":6,"site_name":"qz.com","snippet":"Why vote counting takes days in some states comes down to state law, from mail ballot processing limits to signature checks, curing periods, ...","title":"Why vote counting takes days in some states: 10 reasons","url":"https://qz.com/why-vote-counting-takes-days"},{"date":"Aug 9, 2026","position":7,"site_name":"www.congress.gov","snippet":"Election jurisdictions around the country use various processes and terminology for counting ballots and obtaining election results. The ...","title":"Federal Election Results: Frequently Asked Questions","url":"https://www.congress.gov/crs_external_products/R/PDF/R46565/R46565.9.pdf"},{"position":8,"site_name":"en.wikipedia.org","snippet":"Vote counting is the process of counting votes in an election. It can be done manually or by machines. In the United States, the compilation of election ...","title":"Vote counting","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vote_counting"},{"date":"6 years ago","position":9,"site_name":"www.youtube.com","snippet":"The United States is unique for its lack of a central federalised system to count votes. While rules vary from state to state, in general, ...","title":"How does vote-counting work in the United States?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fgpoeiieuWE"},{"position":10,"site_name":"www.eac.gov","snippet":"The canvass process aggregates and confirms every valid ballot cast and counted, including mail, uniformed and overseas citizen, early voting, Election Day, and ...","title":"Election Results, Canvass, and Certification","url":"https://www.eac.gov/election-officials/election-results-canvass-and-certification"}],"total_results":10,"page":0}